   No big deal. Nethack is all about proper language, and if it can get
English right, it can certainly handle Chinese! The most vexing part,
IMHO, would be coming up with all new puns and maybe even new behaviors
for some actions that no longer make sense in translation. Off the top
of my head --- what would you do with "Undead Turning", which in English
is a pun: "turn" as in "repel", and "turn" as in "become"? AFAIK, that's
not a pun in Chinese. Would you keep the current behaviors of the spell,
and if so, would you try to come up with a replacement pun, or just let
the "strange" behavior go unexplained to the Chinese audience?
   A much less critical but more obvious example: Someone recently 
mentioned the "Isn't that the pits?" pun. That would have to go, too.
   I'd be interested to hear how Spanish Nethack handled the translation
of puns.

