No problem, I think. Besides, the only place the current interface really
lets the /user/ talk about "10 arrows" is in the wishing interface, I
think. And it's already all hacked up to deal with English special cases;
re-hacking it to deal with Chinese would be a breeze by comparison.

   The syntax problems of Chinese would be easily overcome. The hard parts
would be input and output (because in practice they still haven't figured
out whether to use Unicode or Big5 or one of those other encodings whose
names I forget, AFAIK, and input is even less standardized, again AFAIK);
and puns (which would be hard in any language farther away than, say,
French).

